1
00:00:00,070 --> 00:00:03,259
From Calls, select Routes in the top
action bar.

2
00:00:03,750 --> 00:00:07,739
The Routes page lists saved plans and
provides New Route beside

3
00:00:07,769 --> 00:00:09,729
In Progress and Archived Routes.

4
00:00:10,170 --> 00:00:13,850
Begin with New Route for this fictional
community supply exercise.

5
00:00:14,340 --> 00:00:18,780
A named plan gives administrators one
place to prepare the stop sequence and

6
00:00:18,780 --> 00:00:20,950
the information needed at each location.

7
00:00:21,319 --> 00:00:24,450
Use a separate training department when
practicing this process.

8
00:00:24,589 --> 00:00:28,480
Enter a recognizable Name and a
Description that explains the purpose.

9
00:00:28,880 --> 00:00:33,410
Here the name is Community supply loop,
clearly marked training only.

10
00:00:33,820 --> 00:00:37,830
Keep Unit at Assign at start time, and
keep Status at Draft

11
00:00:37,830 --> 00:00:38,980
while preparing the plan.

12
00:00:39,379 --> 00:00:41,639
These are separate fields on Route
Details.

13
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:45,490
Check the department and the plan name
before making changes so the

14
00:00:45,490 --> 00:00:47,500
exercise stays with the intended team.

15
00:00:47,819 --> 00:00:52,319
Review Route Profile, the Avoid checkboxes
and Geofence Radius.

16
00:00:52,770 --> 00:00:57,070
This example keeps Driving, leaves the
Avoid choices clear, and sets the

17
00:00:57,070 --> 00:00:59,020
route radius to one hundred metres.

18
00:00:59,440 --> 00:01:04,329
Check Use Station as Start and Use Station
as End, then select Firehouse

19
00:01:04,329 --> 00:01:06,509
fifty-one in both station selectors.

20
00:01:06,930 --> 00:01:10,999
Optimize Stop Order stays unchecked so we
can review the sequence ourselves.

21
00:01:11,399 --> 00:01:13,089
The stop list is still empty.

22
00:01:13,440 --> 00:01:14,809
Select Add Stop.

23
00:01:14,999 --> 00:01:19,780
In Add Stop, enter Supply point A as the
training Name, choose Manual

24
00:01:19,809 --> 00:01:22,229
as Type, and keep Normal Priority.

25
00:01:22,710 --> 00:01:25,850
The location area says to click the map to
set a location.

26
00:01:26,300 --> 00:01:30,829
Use the map controls to find the intended
area, then select a point and review

27
00:01:30,829 --> 00:01:32,599
the latitude and longitude below it.

28
00:01:33,050 --> 00:01:35,320
The Address here is Chicago, Illinois.

29
00:01:35,759 --> 00:01:38,750
These are fictional exercise points, so
the names do not

30
00:01:38,750 --> 00:01:41,099
identify real service destinations.

31
00:01:41,239 --> 00:01:42,940
Scroll within the stop form.

32
00:01:43,449 --> 00:01:47,480
Leave Planned Arrival and Planned
Departure empty for this exercise, and

33
00:01:47,480 --> 00:01:50,220
enter ten for estimated dwell in minutes.

34
00:01:50,569 --> 00:01:55,179
Leave Arrival radius blank; the help says
a blank uses the route radius.

35
00:01:55,540 --> 00:01:58,409
Select Training Warehouse from Select
Contact.

36
00:01:58,749 --> 00:02:01,380
The contact name and number fill the
fields below.

37
00:02:01,829 --> 00:02:05,490
Review both, then add the training pickup
instruction in Notes.

38
00:02:05,919 --> 00:02:09,550
Select Add Stop to place this prepared
stop in the new route.

39
00:02:09,759 --> 00:02:14,460
Open Add Stop again and name the second
Manual stop Community point B.

40
00:02:14,899 --> 00:02:18,650
Select its own location on the map and
check the displayed coordinates.

41
00:02:19,030 --> 00:02:22,770
In the lower form, enter fifteen minutes
dwell and seventy-five

42
00:02:22,770 --> 00:02:24,409
metres for Arrival radius.

43
00:02:24,719 --> 00:02:29,569
This explicitly supplies a stop-specific
radius instead of leaving the field blank.

44
00:02:29,970 --> 00:02:33,149
Choose the fictional Community Centre
contact, review its

45
00:02:33,149 --> 00:02:36,520
filled name and number, and add the
outreach-supplies note.

46
00:02:36,989 --> 00:02:38,220
Select Add Stop.

47
00:02:38,480 --> 00:02:43,039
Review Stops: the count is now two, with
Supply point A first

48
00:02:43,110 --> 00:02:45,030
and Community point B second.

49
00:02:45,440 --> 00:02:49,389
Check their names, Manual type, address
and Normal priority

50
00:02:49,389 --> 00:02:51,009
before saving the whole plan.

51
00:02:51,469 --> 00:02:53,610
Scroll to Create Route and select it.

52
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:58,449
The returned Routes list now contains
Community supply loop with Draft status,

53
00:02:58,730 --> 00:03:00,830
two stops and the driving profile.

54
00:03:01,230 --> 00:03:05,680
This saved row confirms that the plan was
created beyond the temporary stop form.

55
00:03:05,839 --> 00:03:09,510
Select View for the saved plan and inspect
its two location

56
00:03:09,510 --> 00:03:11,070
pins and the Details panel.

57
00:03:11,539 --> 00:03:15,930
The plan still shows Draft, driving and a
one-hundred-metre geofence.

58
00:03:16,319 --> 00:03:20,930
Select Edit and check the stored Name,
Description, Unit and Status.

59
00:03:21,310 --> 00:03:25,190
Scroll down to verify both Firehouse
fifty-one endpoint selections

60
00:03:25,319 --> 00:03:27,159
and the two saved stop rows.

61
00:03:27,540 --> 00:03:30,950
Reopening checks what Resgrid retained,
rather than relying on

62
00:03:30,950 --> 00:03:32,880
the earlier unsaved selections.

63
00:03:33,039 --> 00:03:37,159
Use the up arrow beside Community point B
in the saved stop list.

64
00:03:37,500 --> 00:03:38,969
It moves to the first row.

65
00:03:39,420 --> 00:03:43,010
Reopen the editor and confirm that this
changed order remains.

66
00:03:43,420 --> 00:03:46,560
These saved-list ordering actions persist
as you use them.

67
00:03:47,060 --> 00:03:50,589
For the supply example, restore pickup
before delivery by

68
00:03:50,589 --> 00:03:52,650
moving Supply point A back up.

69
00:03:53,099 --> 00:03:58,449
Reopen once more and verify Supply point A
first and Community point B second.

70
00:03:58,880 --> 00:04:01,769
Check the actual sequence after every
adjustment.

71
00:04:01,999 --> 00:04:05,669
Open Directions from the saved route row
and review Stop Summary.

72
00:04:06,159 --> 00:04:09,700
Supply point A retains ten minutes dwell,
the Training Warehouse

73
00:04:09,700 --> 00:04:11,430
contact and its pickup note.

74
00:04:11,850 --> 00:04:15,779
Community point B retains fifteen minutes,
its Community Centre

75
00:04:15,779 --> 00:04:17,649
contact and the delivery note.

76
00:04:18,159 --> 00:04:21,930
Above the summary, this example displays
Could not retrieve driving

77
00:04:21,930 --> 00:04:25,930
directions, with guidance to review the
stop addresses or coordinates.

78
00:04:26,329 --> 00:04:29,710
Resolve that warning before relying on the
plan for road guidance.

79
00:04:30,059 --> 00:04:33,350
Saved stops alone do not confirm a
drivable route.

80
00:04:33,579 --> 00:04:37,059
The same preparation pattern can organize
supply stops for search and

81
00:04:37,059 --> 00:04:42,419
rescue, planned security service visits,
wildland contractor support, industrial

82
00:04:42,419 --> 00:04:46,940
emergency logistics, or community
paramedicine and mental health outreach.

83
00:04:47,360 --> 00:04:49,440
Fire and E M S teams can use it too.

84
00:04:50,089 --> 00:04:54,810
Choose appropriate locations and contacts
for your work, allow time at each stop,

85
00:04:55,210 --> 00:04:59,929
verify the saved order, and check the
Directions result before operational use.

86
00:05:00,409 --> 00:05:04,329
A useful plan makes its intended stops and
supporting details easy

87
00:05:04,329 --> 00:05:05,860
for the next person to review.

